## Audit findings — 2026-09-05 (why monthly was inconsistent)

Daily and weekly tiers were healthy (every channel read for 8/31–9/5 had its posts; the only misses
were already caught by fleet-guardian and back-filled). **The monthly tier had no safety net at all:**
none of the monthly publications were in `fleet/expected_outputs.json`, and the guardian's
"ignore anything whose last scheduled fire is >48 h old" rule means a missed 1st-of-month post is
invisible to it by the 3rd. Five distinct failure classes, one per broken publication:

1. **Design flaw** — `monthly-analytics-prestage` (Claude/haiku) ran a 60-min drop→poll→copy loop and
   ended its session before copying; the 6 windows share an end-date filename and overwrote each other.
   Same failure July and August. **Fix:** loop moved to native `bin/monthly_prestage_runner.py`
   (copies from each result.json's `output_path` immediately per window, idempotent, resumable); the
   Cowork task is now launcher + verifier only. Optional launchd plist staged at
   `fleet/com.valleypawn.monthly-prestage.plist` (not installed — needs Joshua's click).
2. **Stale source** — `monthly-employee-sales-rankings` still pointed at a cloud-era shared-folder path;
   the run improvised (data through 8/30, "Total Productivity" instead of Retail Sales Excluding Fees)
   and the post had to be deleted. **Fix:** rebuilt on the pipeline; new additive cell
   `employee-activity-range` (`reports/EmployeeActivityRange.ahk`, +2 lines in `bravo_watcher.ahk`,
   backup `bravo_watcher.ahk.bak-pre-employee-activity-range-2026-09-05`) so the pull is the exact
   calendar month; same metric/format as the weekly board; Rule-18 gate.
3. **Rule 17 violation** — `monthly-scrap-rankings` 9/1 run stopped to object to its own execution
   contract and never pulled. **Fix:** catch-up one-shot 9/5 4:30 PM; guardian coverage added. (A
   Rule-17 preamble for the SKILL.md was drafted at `_pubaudit/scrap.SKILL.md` but not installed.)
4. **Silent death at a non-essential step** — `vp-new-customer-report` died calling the Cowork
   artifact-update tool after the data was complete; the Slack post never happened. **Fix:** August
   posted manually 9/5; SKILL reordered so Slack posts first and the artifact is best-effort.
5. **No monthly summary ever existed** for the other analytics channels and all marketing channels.
   **Fix:** `monthly-eom-recap` (1st 10:30 AM) rolls each channel's own verified weekly/daily posts
   into a Month in Review post in that channel.

Plus the net: **`monthly-publication-audit`** (2nd and 4th, 10 AM) checks every monthly marker for the
prior month and re-runs rerun-safe producers in-session; one plain DM to Joshua only if something can't
be recovered.
